# One ignore file for the whole repo, grouped by REASON (STANDARDS §2) — the reason is
# the documentation of why something is out. Keep new entries in the right group.

# --- Dependencies — reinstalled by `npm install` (the run/server scripts do it for you)
node_modules/

# --- Lockfiles — never tracked: each project generates its own on first `npm install`,
#     so a fresh clone always resolves the newest versions inside each ^range
package-lock.json

# --- Build output — regenerated by `npm run build` (Frontend → Backend/public/dist)
Backend/public/dist/
Frontend/dist/
Frontend/dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Secrets / local config — copy the tracked *.example.json and fill it in locally
Backend/config.json
Frontend/public/config.json
test/test.config.json

# --- Local data — SQLite database files (database.connection.storage)
Backend/data/
*.sqlite
*.local

# --- Test artifacts — regenerated by the UI drives (scripts are tracked, images are not)
test/shots/

# --- Logs — may contain request data (headers, IPs); never commit them
Backend/logs/
logs/
*.log

# --- Generated by the wizard (wizard.bat / wizard.sh) — per-machine launchers
/run_windows.bat
/run_linux.sh
/server_windows.bat
/server_linux.sh

# --- AI docs policy — AI_CarryOn.md + AI_ProgressTracking.md ARE tracked (continuity);
#     template-maintainer notes are not
AI_TemplateCreation.md

# --- Editor / OS
.history/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.sw?
